{
  "description": "Central Limit Theorem engine — pick a population shape (uniform, skewed, bimodal); each draw takes a sample of size n and drops the sample mean into a growing means-histogram that visibly normalizes, with an optional true-mean marker, on a math-canvas. Standalone by default; behind a lab router set matchMode and it renders only when MODE_SELECTED matches.",
